        "patch_url": null
      },
      "commit_id": null,
      "commit_url": null,
      "created_at": "2026-11-05T21:01:21Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-05T21:01:21Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Yes, substituting `POLLIN` for `POLLRDNORM` everywhere would work. I think the bigger issue here is that macOS with poll() returns HUP on a graceful close (when RecvEvent was requested). Versus the current behaviour, this means that because OUT is masked we won't send one last message to the peer before disconnecting. That's probably acceptable, but coupled with the change to immediately disconnect on error [being discussed](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36688#issuecomment-6528271842) (cc @theuni), this means we would drop whatever the peer sent before closing without reading it. That may be acceptable too, though maybe more for p2p than for http, and that's why i opened this issue: it's not clear to me what behaviour we find acceptable, let alone what behaviour we desire.",
      "user": {
        "login": "darosior",
        "id": 22457751,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDU3NzUx",
        "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22457751?v=4",
